title: Kimsuky Defense R&D Lure Shortcut File Creation
id: cd1d7f19-f746-4201-ad56-c3a62ff51f78
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects creation of the Kimsuky lure file reported in November 2026, a
    roughly 70 MB Windows shortcut named to impersonate a 2025 defense-usable
    civilian-held technology report produced by South Korea's Defense
    Technology Promotion Institute. The .lnk masquerades as a PDF and is the
    delivery wrapper for the campaign payload.
references:
    - https://wezard4u.tistory.com/429920
    - https://meterpreter.org/kimsuky-phishing-infrastructure-setup-panel/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/16
tags:
    - attack.t1566
    - attack.t1204
    - attack.t1036
    - attack.t1583
    - attack.t1608
logsource:
    category: file_event
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_lure_name:
        TargetFilename|endswith: '\2025 defense-usable civilian-held technology.pdf.lnk'
    condition: selection_lure_name
falsepositives:
    - Unlikely; the shortcut name is campaign-specific, but a victim organization could receive or copy the same file through benign channels
level: high
